│ patch_description        │ Instead of returning zeros, this implementation runs a deterministic multi-start          │
│                          │ pattern-search (compass search) optimizer directly on the min-triangle-area objective.    │
│                          │ Each starting configuration is generated from a fixed RNG seed; each point is perturbed   │
│                          │ with a geometrically decaying step size, projected back into the equilateral triangle     │
│                          │ (via barycentric clipping), and accepted only if the minimum normalized triangle area     │
│                          │ over all C(11,3)=165 triplets improves. Pattern search is derivative-free, robust to the  │
│                          │ non-smooth min-area objective, deterministic, and converges near locally-optimal          │
│                          │ Heilbronn configurations; multi-start guards against bad local optima. A guaranteed       │
│                          │ feasible fallback (interior points) handles any failure gracefully.                       │
