│                          │ area 0) with a deterministic construction that: (1) initializes 11 points from a          │
│                          │ fixed-seed generator inside the equilateral triangle (vertices included), (2) runs a      │
│                          │ projected gradient-free optimization using scipy's SLSQP on barycentric coordinates (u,v) │
│                          │ with u≥0, v≥0, u+v≤1, so every iterate stays feasible inside the container, and (3)       │
│                          │ maximizes a smooth soft-minimum of all 165 triangle areas with an annealed                │
│                          │ inverse-temperature parameter beta, which approximates the true minimum-area objective    │
│                          │ and escapes poor local minima. Multiple fixed seeds are tried and the configuration with  │
│                          │ the best exact minimum triangle area is returned. All failure paths fall back to a valid  │
│                          │ initial configuration, guaranteeing a feasible (11,2) output. The optimization is fully   │
│                          │ deterministic and runs in a couple of seconds, which is secondary to quality per the      │
│                          │ metrics.                                                                                  │
