│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ worst_point_refiner                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Key weakness: the current refiner perturbs all 22 coordinates at once, so a random step   │
│                          │ almost never improves the *global* minimum triangle (which is what the score is). Expert  │
│                          │ practice for maximin geometry optimization is to (a) identify the point(s) participating  │
│                          │ in the smallest-area triangles and perturb only those (coordinate descent on the binding  │
│                          │ constraints), and (b) use a geometric annealing of step sizes with occasional larger      │
│                          │ restarts. This makes each accepted move directly relax the bottleneck triangle instead of │
│                          │ randomly shuffling the whole configuration. I also increase the number of curated seeds   │
│                          │ (vertices pinned plus a symmetric sublattice, which is a strong inductive bias for        │
│                          │ Heilbronn-type problems) while keeping everything deterministic. The change is purely in  │
│                          │ the refine loop and seed list, so the fallback and geometry kernel remain untouched and   │
│                          │ the program still runs if anything fails.                                                 │
