│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ global_moves_escape_local_optima                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The single-point random moves get trapped in local optima because moving one point at a   │
│                          │ time cannot restructure the whole configuration. I add a global "shake all points" phase: │
│                          │ random displacement of all points at once with a moderate sigma, accept if min_area       │
│                          │ improves (or via annealing). Repeating this between local refinement rounds lets the      │
│                          │ search hop between basins. Also add a final alternating pattern polish: for each point,   │
│                          │ try a small set of axis-aligned and diagonal moves greedily, which reliably squeezes out  │
│                          │ extra area after the stochastic phases.                                                   │
