│ patch_name               │ random_dir_anneal_bottleneck                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Inspired by the recommendation to replace fixed directional fans with randomized          │
│                          │ directions, and by the prior programs' barycentric-simplex formulation and                │
│                          │ bottleneck-focused hill climbing, this implementation uses a multi-restart annealer in    │
│                          │ (u,v) simplex coordinates. Key novel elements: (1) each sweep draws ~8 fresh random       │
│                          │ directions per candidate point (isotropic Gaussian in barycentric space, then             │
│                          │ simplex-projected), letting the search slip through asymmetric gaps; (2) moves target     │
│                          │ only the points appearing in triangles near the current minimum (bottleneck points),      │
│                          │ computed vectorized via a soft-threshold mask rather than a slow Python loop over         │
│                          │ triples; (3) a geometric temperature schedule with restarts from jittered lattice seeds,  │
│                          │ keeping only the best result. Fully deterministic via fixed seeds, with a feasible static │
│                          │ fallback.                                                                                 │
