│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ bottleneck_gradient_lift                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Inspired by the prior annealers, but replaces blind random moves with a targeted "lift"   │
│                          │ step: repeatedly identify the single bottleneck triangle (smallest area) and analytically │
│                          │ move its three vertices along the gradient of the signed area to inflate it, with         │
│                          │ backtracking line search and simplex projection. Annealing kicks only fire on stalls, so  │
│                          │ iterations are spent where the objective is binding. A strict non-degeneracy floor (min   │
│                          │ area > 0.5 * fallback value) plus multi-start over perturbed lattice seeds guarantees a   │
│                          │ valid, non-degenerate result, addressing the silent-zero failures of earlier generations. │
