│ patch_name               │ nonzero_floor_and_more_starts                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current multi-start keeps the best across only 6 seeds, and if all refinements are    │
│                          │ weak (or degenerate) it silently returns a low-scoring configuration. Two targeted fixes: │
│                          │ (1) increase the number of multi-start seeds to explore more of the landscape (the known  │
│                          │ best Heilbronn 11-point configurations are hard to reach from a lattice start, so more    │
│                          │ restarts with varied perturbation scales helps); (2) add an explicit non-degeneracy       │
│                          │ floor: any candidate whose min area is below 0.01 is rejected, and if no candidate passes │
│                          │ the floor, the function retries with fresh seeds instead of returning a degenerate/weak   │
│                          │ result. This guarantees the returned configuration always has a meaningful nonzero        │
│                          │ minimum triangle area while improving expected quality.                                   │
