│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multistart_anneal_repulsion                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The key bottleneck is initialization diversity: all seeds derive from two order-3 lattice │
│                          │ layouts. The new program adds three seed families: (1) electrostatic repulsion layouts    │
│                          │ (points pushed apart inside the triangle via deterministic force iterations), (2)         │
│                          │ golden-ratio asymmetric low-discrepancy jitter layouts, (3) original lattice seeds. Each  │
│                          │ seed is refined by a faster annealer with an adaptive temperature schedule (T0=0.02       │
│                          │ geometric decay to 1e-5) and a cheap local coordinate-descent polish pass at the end that │
│                          │ tries small axis-aligned moves on the bottleneck point only, which is where the last      │
│                          │ gains typically come from. Vectorized area computation and cached triples keep eval time  │
│                          │ low. More diverse seeds plus the polish stage raise min_area while staying within a few   │
│                          │ seconds.                                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0161                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
