├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ bottleneck_correlated_lift                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Key parameters of the current approach: 6 lattice seeds, 12-direction single-point        │
│                          │ pattern search with geometric step schedule (0.04→0.0005), uniform point selection, and a │
│                          │ min-area objective handled only through single-point moves. This gets stuck easily        │
│                          │ because the bottleneck triangle typically needs all three of its vertices moved together. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New configuration:                                                                        │
│                          │ 1. **Bottleneck-membership weighted coordinated moves**: compute membership counts of     │
│                          │ each point in the K smallest-area triangles (K≈8), then move the top-1, top-2, or top-3   │
│                          │ bottleneck points simultaneously along analytic area-gradient directions (converting      │
│                          │ xy-gradients to barycentric directions), with backtracking line search — this implements  │
│                          │ the recommended correlated multi-point moves.                                             │
│                          │ 2. **Adaptive annealing kick**: when line search stalls, apply a correlated jitter whose  │
│                          │ magnitude decays geometrically (sigma *= 0.7), accepted simulated-annealing style,        │
│                          │ escaping single-point traps deterministically (fixed seeds).                              │
│                          │ 3. **Final pattern-search polish** at small steps to squeeze remaining gains.             │
│                          │ 4. Multi-start over 8 seeds with a safe quality floor; fallback to best-of-seeds rather   │
│                          │ than raising (the prior gradient program scored 0.00 likely because an over-strict floor  │
│                          │ triggered the fallback — this is fixed by always returning the best found configuration). │
│                          │ 5. Vectorized area evaluation with precomputed triplet indices keeps runtime modest (~3–6 │
│                          │ s).                                                                                       │
