│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ boundary_seed_and_faster_refine                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Expert knowledge on the Heilbronn problem: for small n (n=11), the best known             │
│                          │ configurations (Goldberg-style) place most or all points on the boundary of the convex    │
│                          │ region — collinear triples on edges are avoided by using different spacings on each side, │
│                          │ and boundary placement maximizes the "spread" that drives up the minimum triangle area.   │
│                          │ The current code only perturbs an interior lattice, which caps the achievable minimum     │
│                          │ area. I add a boundary-heavy deterministic seed generator (points distributed along the   │
│                          │ three edges with slightly different, golden-ratio-based spacings to avoid near-collinear  │
│                          │ triples), feed those seeds through the existing refine loop, and cut the seed budget from │
│                          │ 30 to a smaller mixed set (10 lattice + 6 boundary) to keep eval_time low while focusing  │
│                          │ the search on the more promising boundary configurations.                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
