│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two approaches: keep the fast vectorized softmin-annealed Adam gradient  │
│                          │ ascent (from script 2 / current program) as the main optimizer, but replace its purely    │
│                          │ random initialization with the perturbed triangular-lattice seeds from script 3 (which    │
│                          │ scored best, 0.55). After each Adam run, apply the deterministic multi-direction local    │
│                          │ polish (from script 3) but only on the bottleneck point(s) to keep it cheap (inspired by  │
│                          │ script 1's bottleneck-focused polish). Multi-start over a few lattice seeds, keep the     │
│                          │ best exact min-area configuration, with a guaranteed feasible lattice fallback. This      │
│                          │ should match or beat 0.55 combined score at lower runtime than the 2.67s pure             │
│                          │ local-search version.                                                                     │
