│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ golden_and_repulsion_seeds                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The prior evidence (Gen 17/22) shows that all current seeds are perturbed copies of the   │
│                          │ same symmetric order-3 triangular lattice, so the annealing multistart gets trapped in    │
│                          │ the same symmetry-biased basin — every seed produces essentially the same local optimum.  │
│                          │ I add two fundamentally different seed families:                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. A **golden-ratio low-discrepancy seed**: barycentric coordinates built from fractional │
│                          │ parts of (k·φ, k·φ²), giving a highly uniform, asymmetric initial layout with no lattice  │
│                          │ collinearity to fight against.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. A **repulsion seed**: ~60 vectorized inverse-square repulsion iterations from a        │
│                          │ jittered layout, projected back with `_clip` after each step. This spreads points toward  │
│                          │ a well-separated configuration, which is exactly what large minimum triangle areas        │
│                          │ require (near-uniform point spacing).                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Since these new seeds start from different basins, they give the annealer a real chance   │
│                          │ to find a better optimum rather than re-confirming the lattice basin. To keep total       │
│                          │ runtime in budget (the current version already takes 15s, which is costly for eval_time), │
│                          │ I slightly reduce the number of lattice seeds (8 → 4) since they are highly redundant     │
│                          │ with each other, freeing time for the two new asymmetric seeds. All methods remain fully  │
│                          │ deterministic (fixed seeds, vectorized numpy), and the fallback behavior is unchanged.    │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0095                                                                                   │
