│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ bottleneck_symmetric_hybrid                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Both prior programs plateau at combined_score 0.39, indicating the randomized jitter      │
│                          │ local search gets stuck in poor local optima. The crossover combines the faster           │
│                          │ random-search skeleton (program 1) with the bottleneck-targeted polish (program 2), and   │
│                          │ adds two key improvements: (1) structured symmetric seeds (near-uniform lattice           │
│                          │ arrangements known to be strong starting points for Heilbronn-type problems, e.g.         │
│                          │ hexagonal/perturbed-lattice placements), and (2) an aggressive "bottleneck relief" move   │
│                          │ that pushes all three vertices of the worst triangle away from its centroid, which        │
│                          │ escapes local optima that single-point jitter cannot. Multi-scale descent (coarse jitter  │
│                          │ → bottleneck polish → micro jitter) with fewer seeds keeps runtime near the faster        │
│                          │ variant while searching deeper. Deterministic seeds and the same fallback guarantee       │
│                          │ identical interface and robustness.                                                       │
