                        Patch Metadata - Gen 43/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ pairwise_bottleneck_polish                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The tightest bottleneck in Heilbronn-11 configurations is typically a small cluster of    │
│                          │ 3-4 points whose triangles bind simultaneously. Single-point moves cannot escape these    │
│                          │ "pair-traps" because moving either point alone decreases the min area even though moving  │
│                          │ both together increases it. I replace the random-jitter final polish in `_refine` with a  │
│                          │ structured greedy polish that (a) identifies the top-2 bottleneck triangles, (b) tries    │
│                          │ moving their involved points individually AND simultaneously along 12 fixed directions    │
│                          │ (plus opposites), and (c) continues scanning remaining directions at the same step size   │
│                          │ after an improvement before shrinking. This gives the optimizer a mechanism to escape     │
│                          │ coordinated constraints, which should raise the achievable min area. Since only           │
│                          │ bottleneck-involved points are moved (not all 11 × 12 directions), per-iteration cost     │
│                          │ stays modest, and the random 200-sample loop (which wastes evaluations on irrelevant      │
│                          │ points) is removed, recovering runtime.                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0128                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ z-ai/glm-5.3                                                                              │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ reasoning                │ {'effort': 'low'}                                                                         │
