│                          │ recomputes all 165 triplet areas (plus full-array indexing `_min_area`). Since a          │
│                          │ candidate only moves one point, only the ~90 triplets containing that point change.       │
│                          │ Precompute, per point index, the rows of `_TRIP` containing it, maintain a full area      │
│                          │ (cross-magnitude) vector, and update only the affected entries per candidate — then take  │
│                          │ the min over the updated vector. This cuts candidate evaluation cost roughly 2×, letting  │
│                          │ us afford a richer candidate set (24 directions including the normalized gradient of the  │
│                          │ bottleneck triangle) and trying all 11 points (not just the top-3 by tight-count) within  │
│                          │ the same sub-second runtime, which increases the chance of escaping local minima and      │
│                          │ pushing min_area higher. The `while improved` loop's tight-count bookkeeping is retained  │
│                          │ but computed from the maintained area vector, so it costs nothing extra.                  │
