                        Patch Metadata - Gen 48/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_smooth_gradient_adam_stage                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current greedy jitter search plateaus at min_area 0.01 (score 0.39). The bottleneck   │
│                          │ is that greedy single-point moves cannot coordinate all 11 points simultaneously. A much  │
│                          │ better approach for this kind of max-min problem is to optimize a smooth surrogate of the │
│                          │ min: the softmin log-sum-exp over all 165 triangle doubled-areas, whose gradient w.r.t.   │
│                          │ the barycentric coordinates is computable in closed form via vectorized numpy. Running    │
│                          │ Adam on this smooth objective pushes area values into near-degeneracy (many triangles     │
│                          │ near the min), then we harden the temperature (lower softmin sharpness) and finish with   │
│                          │ the existing local search as a polish step. This directly attacks the plateau and is the  │
│                          │ classic way to escape greedy local optima in Heilbronn-style packing problems.            │
