│ patch_description        │ The expensive simulated annealing keeps stalling at 0.02 while consuming most of the 9s   │
│                          │ budget. Replace it with a smooth-minimum (log-sum-exp) Adam gradient ascent on all 165    │
│                          │ triangle areas simultaneously: the softmin relaxation gives gradient signal to *every*    │
│                          │ bottleneck triplet at once, which random single-point perturbation lacks. Adam            │
│                          │ re-homogenizes the area distribution, then the existing `_polish` sharpens it. Wrap this  │
│                          │ in a cheap outer loop (Adam → polish → reheat Adam → polish, keeping the best), per the   │
│                          │ recommendation. This directly attacks the 0.02 plateau with gradient information instead  │
│                          │ of blind search.                                                                          │
