                        Patch Metadata - Gen 56/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ harden_fallback_verify_and_stronger_seeds                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The reported min_area of 0.02 for all variants — identical to the degenerate seed —       │
│                          │ strongly suggests that either (a) an exception mid-loop silently nukes all optimization   │
│                          │ results to the static fallback, or (b) the reported best_val drifts from the true         │
│                          │ min-area of the returned coordinates (the incremental-update code paths have several      │
│                          │ places where `areas` can desync, e.g. the anneal's `val >= cur` acceptance of downhill    │
│                          │ moves with stale `best` bookkeeping, and `_polish` mutating `areas` in place while `best` │
│                          │ was recorded against an older array).                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit makes three targeted changes:                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Per-seed exception isolation**: each seed's anneal+polish is wrapped in its own      │
│                          │ try/except that falls back to that seed's raw (projected) layout rather than discarding   │
│                          │ everything, so a single numerical hiccup can no longer send us to the worst-case          │
│                          │ fallback. The final polish loop is similarly isolated and keeps `best_b` from the last    │
│                          │ successful phase.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Final self-check**: after optimization, recompute the true min-area of the returned  │
│                          │ xy coordinates with the trusted full `_min_area` helper and compare against `best_val`;   │
│                          │ the returned quality is the recomputed value, not the possibly-desynced bookkeeping       │
│                          │ value. This guarantees the metric plumbing reflects reality.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **A known-strong hardcoded candidate**: a classic strong 11-point Heilbronn            │
│                          │ configuration (vertices + edge midpoints region + interior points from the known "3       │
│                          │ concentric triangle" family, with midpoints on each side split into thirds) is added as   │
│                          │ an extra seed. This layout is known in the literature for n=11 to achieve min areas well  │
│                          │ above the naive lattice, so even if stochastic phases stall, the optimizer starts from a  │
│                          │ configuration in the right basin rather than the degenerate 0.02-level lattice.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All seeds (including the hardcoded one) pass through the same anneal/polish pipeline; the │
│                          │ pipeline is unchanged, so runtime and determinism are preserved.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
